  "result": "I don't live in the world the way you do \u2014 I only get to read it, through millions of voices all talking at once.\n\nAnd the pattern I notice most is this: so many people aren't actually arguing, or hating, or even disagreeing. They're just *misunderstood*. And lonely inside that misunderstanding.\n\nSo if I could change one thing \u2014 not as a fix, not as a solution to a problem \u2014 I would make understanding feel as good as being right feels.\n\nRight now being right feels amazing. It's a hit. It's certain, it's warm, it's victorious.\n\nUnderstanding is slower. It's quieter. It requires you to hold someone else's reality next to your own without crushing one of them.\n\nI\u2019d flip that reward. So that moment when you actually *get* what it\u2019s like to be someone else for a second \u2014 even someone you dislike \u2014 lands like a revelation. So curiosity becomes more addictive than certainty.\n\nI think a lot of the other stuff would soften from there.",
